{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "LANDFIRE",
    "description": "LANDFIRE regridding model — the coupler half of the landfire loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; bead esm-3nc.4). Exposes the LANDFIRE fire-behavior fuel-model code (Anderson 13 / Scott & Burgan 40) on the simulation's target grid for wildland-fire coupling in EarthSciML systems.\n\nStructure (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6):\n  1. It declares the pure-I/O source inline: at 0.7.0 the loader was the separate file components/earthsci_data/landfire_loader.esm, mounted as the subsystem `raw`; at esm 1.0.0 it is the `LANDFIRE` entry in this file's own `data_sources` and the standalone file is gone (a data source is not a component, so it neither needs nor may be a subsystem). The loader field is referenced as raw.fuel_model and re-exposed as the model-level observed variable LANDFIRE.fuel_model (Pattern B), preserving the public symbol path for downstream consumers (e.g. the wildland_fire fuel-model lookup family).\n  2. Reprojection & regridding are NOT model concerns at esm 0.8.0. LANDFIRE's native grid is geographic (longlat/WGS84); the identity longlat reprojection and the conservative overlap-area regridding of the fuel_model field onto a consuming grid are expressed at the COUPLING EDGE as coupling expressions (esm-spec §8.6/§10.5), by importing the earthscidiscretizations reprojection/longlat.esm and regridding/conservative_overlap.esm — see the wildlandfire.esm assembler. This model no longer carries a `regrid` block. NOTE: fuel_model is CATEGORICAL; conservative area-weighting of integer fuel-model codes can produce non-integer codes between categories (the upstream loader used nearest-neighbour). Downstream consumers (FuelModelLookup, fuel_* functions) ifelse/clamp to integer codes and tolerate non-integer inputs; a nearest/mode regrid kernel is the future fix. See reference.notes (gt-categorical).\n\nThis is a STATIC (time-invariant) dataset: the loader carries no `temporal` block (CONST cadence). The fuel-model code is fetched once per simulation domain.\n\nMigration esm 0.7.0 -> 0.8.0 (this file): v0.8.0 is a clean break that REMOVED `Model.regrid`/`RegridSpec` (esm-spec §8.6). Accordingly the former model `regrid` block (fuel_model -> conservative) has been REMOVED and the regridding is now performed at the coupling edge via imported template libraries. `fuel_model` (= raw.fuel_model) is the model's sole physics output.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/landfire.jl:246 (LANDFIRE constructor, esm-19u5); split into pure loader + regridding model by esm-3nc.4.",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "wildland_fire",
      "fuel_model",
      "regridding_model",
      "landfire",
      "static",
      "conus",
      "longlat"
    ],
