  "models": {
    "LANDFIRE": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "source_ref: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/landfire.jl:246\n\nThis is the regridding-model half of the pure-IO loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7, bead esm-3nc.4). The pre-migration landfire.esm carried both the coupler model AND a co-located data_loaders.LANDFIRE block (with the now-removed `spatial` and `regridding` sub-blocks). That loader became, at 0.7.0, the pure-I/O file components/earthsci_data/landfire_loader.esm, referenced as subsystem `raw`; at esm 1.0.0 it is the `LANDFIRE` entry in THIS file's `data_sources` and the standalone file is gone.\n\nUpstream constructor LANDFIRE(domaininfo; name=:LANDFIRE, product=\"FBFM13\", version=\"LF2022\", resolution=1.0, stream=true, spatial_interp=:linear) created an MTK System with:\n  - @parameters: lon (rad), lat (rad) from domaininfo pvars (via pvdict)\n  - One observed equation via create_interp_equation(itp, \"\", t, t_ref, [lon, lat]; spatial_interp)\n    where itp = DataSetInterpolator{dt}(FileSetWithRegridder(fs, regrid_f), \"fuel_model\", ...)\n    and fs = LANDFIREFileSet(domaininfo; product, version, resolution)\n    and regrid_f uses _nearest_interpolate_from! (BSpline(Constant())) for categorical data\n  - discrete_events: build_interp_event fires at simulation start (static dataset)\n  - metadata: Dict(CoupleType => LANDFIRECoupler, SysDomainInfo => domaininfo)\nThese loader fields are now provided by the loader subsystem `raw` (raw.fuel_model) and re-exposed as the model observed variable fuel_model.\n\nReprojection (RFC §6 step 2): LANDFIRE's native grid.crs.projection is 'longlat', so the reprojection rule selected by convention is the identity ESD reprojection/longlat.esm (esd-47z.1). The model does not name the ESD file; it only requires the loader's crs to be correct.\n\nRegridding (RFC §6 step 3 / §5.2): declared per variable in the model `regrid` block. The cell-centered fuel_model field → conservative area-weighted overlap join (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm), per the esm-3nc.4 migration spec (cell-centered → conservative).\n\nCATEGORICAL REGRID GAP (gt-categorical, carried forward per gotcha §8): the upstream loader used NEAREST-NEIGHBOUR interpolation (_nearest_interpolate_from!, BSpline(Constant())) precisely because fuel_model is categorical — area-weighted averaging of integer fuel-model codes is not physically meaningful (the average of code 1 and code 13 is code 7, an unrelated category). The new ESS RegridSpec.method enum offers only {conservative, bspline, cell_average}; there is no nearest/mode kernel. Per the migration spec this model declares conservative. Downstream consumers (components/wildland_fire/fuel_model_lookup.esm; the fuel_* registered functions) ifelse/clamp to integer codes and tolerate non-integer inputs, but the categorical semantics are best served by a future nearest/mode regrid kernel in ESS. When such a kernel lands, switch regrid.fuel_model.method to it.\n\nStaticness: no `temporal` block on the loader → CONST cadence. The GeoTIFF is fetched once per simulation domain; upstream DataFrequencyInfo uses a single interval spanning [starttime, endtime + 1 day] and build_interp_event fires once at starttime.\n\nNote on projections: the upstream _domain_bbox_wgs84 handles both longlat and projected (e.g. LCC) domains by transforming all edge points to WGS84 to compute the bounding envelope. The loader's native grid is geographic regardless of the target domain's projection; the runtime computes the request bbox from the target domain envelope."
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-06
      },
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's longitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's latitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem."
        },
        "fuel_model": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "LANDFIRE fire behavior fuel model code at the model grid point. Sourced from the loader field raw.fuel_model and regridded onto the target grid. Valid FBFM13 values: 0 (no fuel), 1–13 (Anderson 13 burnable models), 91=urban/developed, 92=snow/ice, 93=agriculture, 98=water, 99=barren. FBFM40 adds codes 101–204. CATEGORICAL: non-integer values may appear after conservative regridding (see regrid.fuel_model); downstream consumers (FuelModelLookup, fuel_* functions) round/clamp to integer codes via ifelse + interp.linear. Static (time-invariant): the same value is returned for all simulation times.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "LANDFIRE",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "Band1",
              "description": "Fire behavior fuel model code (categorical integer). Raw GeoTIFF pixel type S16; TiffImages reads as Q0f15 fixed-point — multiply by 32768 to recover integer fuel model codes. For FBFM13 (Anderson 13): codes 0 (no fuel), 1–13 (burnable), 91=urban, 92=snow/ice, 93=agriculture, 98=water, 99=barren. For FBFM40 (Scott & Burgan 40): codes 101–204 additional. Coverage: contiguous United States (CONUS) only. This is CATEGORICAL data — see metadata.interpolation_note and the regridding model's regrid.fuel_model description for the regridding-kernel consideration."
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "equations": [],
      "tests": []
    }
  }
}
